      "page": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "bbox": [
        213,
        710,
        784,
        773
      ],
      "text": "In probability theory, if \\( X \\sim N(\\mu, \\sigma^2) \\), then the expected value \\( \\mathbb{E}[X] = \\mu \\) and the variance \\( \\operatorname{Var}(X) = \\sigma^2 \\). The standard normal distribution has the density function \\( \\phi(x) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}} e^{-x^2/2} \\), and its cumulative distribution function is denoted by \\( \\Phi(x) \\)."
    },
