      "page": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "bbox": [
        213,
        774,
        784,
        835
      ],
      "text": "For vectors in \\(\\mathbb{R}^n\\), the dot product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} u_i v_i\\) measures the angle between vectors, while the norm \\(\\| \\mathbf{v} \\|_2 = \\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} v_i^2}\\) gives the Euclidean length. A matrix \\(A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}\\) is orthogonal if \\(A^T A = I_n\\), where \\(I_n\\) is the \\(n \\times n\\) identity matrix."
    },
    {
